    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Production Environment Stability Hardening\"... okay, yeah, that sounds much more official than \"fighting ghosts.\" i'll definitely use that.\n\nit's just hard to explain how much time it's actually eating. it's not even one big thing every time; it's like these little, annoying, chaotic little hiccups that just seem to live in the system. they appear, cause a mess, and then scurry back into the code before we can even catch them. it's like a constant stream of tiny, mischievous little disruptions that are just hanging out in the shadows of our infrastructure. \n\ndo you have any more ways to describe that specific feeling of these tiny, disorganized, nearly invisible things just causing havoc and messing with our things? i want to convey that the problem isn't our code itself, but these little uninvited guests that just won't stay away.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
