      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Non-Deterministic State Drift\"... right, yeah, i'll put that in the report. it sounds exactly like what's happening.\n\nbut i'm still struggling with how to communicate the *vibe* of it to the team. they're getting so burnt out because it feels like we're being picked at by a swarm of tiny, little pests. it's not like we're facing a dragon or something—it's just these endless, small, annoying, and slightly chaotic little things that seem to be lurking in the corners of our architecture, just waiting to trip us up.\n\ndo you get what i mean? it's just this feeling of these little, uninvited, chaotic entities that just exist to cause minor havoc. is there any professional way to describe that kind of \"little, mischievous force\" that keeps disrupting everything? i don't want to sound like i'm making up monsters, but the way it behaves is so... unpredictable and almost spiteful.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
